CORE
main.c
--dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts
^main.c.*error: decreases clause component must have arithmetic type, but has type 'signed int \*'$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^EXIT=(1|64)$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
A decreases clause is compared with the strict arithmetic order (or, for
several components, the lexicographic order), so each of its components must
have arithmetic type. A pointer component used to be accepted, and the
comparison then did not express termination.
